# AutoTuneX — LSF runner example configuration (granite.build, standalone/SkyPilot)
#
# Runner: the granite.build LSF/SkyPilot launcher (AUTOTUNEX_JOB_BACKEND=llmb
# together with GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone AND AUTOTUNEX_LSF_CLUSTER set). Emits
# the space://steps/autotunex-tune build.yaml with a skypilot: config block and
# submits it through the llmb CLI to run the tuning sweep on an LSF cluster.
#
# Selection: under GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone the launcher emits the local-bash
# spec by DEFAULT; setting AUTOTUNEX_LSF_CLUSTER switches it to this LSF spec.
#
# Use it:
#   export GB_TOKEN=<your gb token>     # REQUIRED — see the note below
#   export HF_TOKEN=<your hf token>     # REQUIRED — datasets are HF-hosted
#   cp envs/lsf.env.example .env
#   # fill in the required LSF inputs below, then:
#   make dev
#
# GB_TOKEN must be EXPORTED into the shell, not merely written here: the
# reconcile loop authenticates to gbserver with it over HTTP, and startup
# refuses to run if the variable is absent (its value is never read into
# Settings). HF_TOKEN is required the same way once dataset storage is
# huggingface (below).
#
# Runtime prerequisite: datasets must be HuggingFace-hosted (the build
# references them by hf:// URI).
#
# This file covers what the LSF runner needs. For everything else — the optional
# auth providers (OIDC / BFF / API keys), serving the built UI, dataset-preview
# tuning, and the LLM-intelligence feature — see the full menu in the root
# .env.example. Every AUTOTUNEX_ variable is documented in
# src/autotunex/core/config.py.
# Runner design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-13-lsf-runner-design.md

# --- Application -----------------------------------------------------------
AUTOTUNEX_APP_NAME="AutoTuneX API"
# dev | test | prod
AUTOTUNEX_ENVIRONMENT=dev
AUTOTUNEX_DEBUG=false
AUTOTUNEX_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
AUTOTUNEX_API_PREFIX=/api/v1

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite for local development; no server needed.
AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:///./autotunex.db
AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_ECHO=false
# Create missing tables on startup (dev convenience; use `make migrate` in prod).
AUTOTUNEX_AUTO_CREATE_SCHEMA=true

# --- Artifact storage ------------------------------------------------------
AUTOTUNEX_ARTIFACT_DIR=./artifacts

# --- Auth (standalone / dev) -----------------------------------------------
# A JSON array, NOT a comma-separated list. "disabled" is standalone mode: every
# caller is the same principal. Leaving STANDALONE_EMAIL unset attributes writes
# to a default system owner (standalone@autotunex.local).
AUTOTUNEX_AUTH_PROVIDERS=["disabled"]
# AUTOTUNEX_STANDALONE_EMAIL=you@example.com
AUTOTUNEX_STANDALONE_ROLE=admin
# AUTOTUNEX_AUTO_PROVISION_USERS=true

# --- Execution: the LSF/SkyPilot launcher (granite.build standalone) --------
# JOB_BACKEND=llmb selects the llmb launcher; GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone is the
# standalone mode; AUTOTUNEX_LSF_CLUSTER (below) switches the emitted spec from
# local-bash to LSF/SkyPilot.
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_BACKEND=llmb
# NOTE: GB_ENVIRONMENT is granite.build's own variable and is UNPREFIXED (no
# AUTOTUNEX_).
GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone

# The SkyPilot/LSF cluster name (launcher_config.resources.cluster). REQUIRED and
# the DISCRIMINATOR — setting it selects the LSF spec over the bash spec.
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_CLUSTER=example-cluster
# granite.build space environment for the LSF build. REQUIRED.
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_ENVIRONMENT_URI=space://environments/skypilot/lsf/example-cluster
# Runtime container image the LSF step runs in (skypilot.image). REQUIRED.
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_IMAGE=registry.example.com/tuner:1
# SkyPilot accelerators string (resources.accelerators), e.g. "H100:2". Leaving
# it unset produces a 0-GPU build.
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_ACCELERATORS=H100:2
# LSF queue (resources.zone). Optional.
# AUTOTUNEX_LSF_QUEUE=normal
# Requested memory (resources.memory). Optional.
# AUTOTUNEX_LSF_MEMORY=256+
# skypilot.venv_path — where the runtime image installs torch/ray.
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_VENV_PATH=/step_venv
# CUDA toolkit path exported in the start command (present on the runtime image).
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_CUDA_HOME=/opt/share/cuda-12.9
# compute_config sizing.
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_NUM_CPUS_PER_NODE=32
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_TOTAL_MEMORY_PER_NODE=256Gi
# The step's poll_interval_seconds / log_retrieval_interval_seconds.
AUTOTUNEX_LSF_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=30

# Trainer source repository the build checks out (github_url/github_ref).
# REQUIRED in LSF mode.
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_TRAINER_REPO=https://github.example.com/org/fm-tune.git
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_TRAINER_REF=main

# Base URL of the local gbserver the reconcile loop polls. REQUIRED — without it
# an accepted job sits "pending" forever.
AUTOTUNEX_GB_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:9000

# Name of the env var holding the gb auth token (see the export note above).
AUTOTUNEX_GB_TOKEN_ENV=GB_TOKEN

# The llmb CLI binary name or path used to submit builds.
AUTOTUNEX_LLMB_COMMAND=llmb

# Where the generated build.yaml is written (<dir>/<job_id>/build.yaml).
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_SPEC_DIR=tmp

# Base URL a cluster worker reports back to (optional; the LSF build only emits
# --autotunex_server_url when this is set).
# AUTOTUNEX_JOB_CALLBACK_URL=https://api.example.com

# How often the reconcile loop sweeps non-terminal jobs, and the per-sweep read cap.
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECONDS=30
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_RECONCILE_CONCURRENCY=5

# --- Dataset storage (HuggingFace backend) ---------------------------------
# The LSF build references datasets by hf:// URI, so datasets must be pushed to
# HuggingFace. Forcing "huggingface" fails startup unless BOTH GB_TOKEN and
# HF_TOKEN are exported (checked at startup; the values never enter Settings).
AUTOTUNEX_DATASET_STORAGE_BACKEND=huggingface
# Optional HF org/namespace prefix for the pushed dataset repo.
# AUTOTUNEX_HF_NAMESPACE=your-org
